+Owner skill: `skill://rust-conventions`. A merge request's merge in the user's own checkout (plan §2 #139–#143, request `docs/slices/request-mr-conflicts.md` rules 4–10, design `docs/slices/briefs/mr-conflicts-design.md` §4.2–§4.6); depends on `yamt-gitio` only among yamt crates, never on tauri or GitLab (`scripts/arch-check.sh`). `lib.rs` (the IPC types `Started`, `Refusal`, `ReturnTo`, `Leftover`, `BranchBefore`, `MergeView`, `LocalMerge` (`merging` with `windowOpen`), `PushReply`; `MergeRequestBranches`, `PushOffer`, `LiveMerge` (`view`, `iid`, `restore`, `committed`), `WindowClaim`; `Error`; `local_merge`, `find_live`, `claim_window` (`try_lock` every 50 ms for up to 1 s), `window_is_open` (one `try_lock`, released at once); `git_message`: git's first stderr line), `record.rs` (the record `<git dir>/yamt-merge-request.json` through `Repo::git_path`, format 1: `MergeRecord`, `RecordedReturn`, `RecordedBranch`, never on the IPC; `read` (a newer format or unparsable JSON is `Err` with the reason), `write` (temp file, `sync_all`, rename), `remove`; `hold`, the `File::try_lock` of the start lock `yamt-merge-request.lock` and the window lock `yamt-merge-window.lock`, both never removed; `is_live`: git merging the recorded commit at the recorded head on the recorded branch), `start.rs` (`start`: design §4.2's thirteen steps in order — discover, start lock, the record (live → `AlreadyMerging`, unreadable → `RecordUnreadable` and kept, stale → removed), any operation → `Busy`, tracked changes, `fetch_branches`, the two remote-tracking tips, the local branch (created / unchanged / moved from / `LocalAhead`), `AlreadyContains`, the return place, the record written, `checkout -B` (refused → record removed, nothing changed), the upstream of a created branch, `merge --no-ff --no-commit <remote>/<target>` (the full `refs/remotes/…` when another ref has that short name), live afterwards or restored; any other git error before the checkout is `GitRefused` with `left` empty), `restore.rs` (`restore`: back to the branch or commit while HEAD is still the branch at the recorded head, then the created branch deleted or the moved one moved back (`branch --force`, or `reset --keep` when checked out) while it is still at that head; what does not match is a `Leftover`; the record removed), `push.rs` (`push`: `push_branch` to the recorded remote, `PUSH_TIMEOUT`). Tests: `tests/local_merge/` (one binary; `common.rs` builds `scripts/mr-conflict-repo.sh`'s repository and its fake GitLab), units in `record.rs` and `lib.rs`.
